            "text": "{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"q1\",\"conclusion\":\"yes\",\"answer\":\"The operator is responsible for ensuring the restraint system is properly secured, and it must be secured to an approved forward-facing seat or berth when a child occupies an approved child restraint system under 14 CFR § 91.107(a)(3)(iii).\",\"support_refs\":[\"statement\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[]},{\"question_id\":\"q2\",\"conclusion\":\"no\",\"answer\":\"No. The requirement specifically applies when a child occupies an approved child restraint system under 14 CFR § 91.107(a)(3)(iii), not whenever any child restraint exists anywhere or outside aircraft.\",\"support_refs\":[\"statement\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[]},{\"question_id\":\"q3\",\"conclusion\":\"no\",\"answer\":\"No. The supplied material references only 14 CFR § 91.107(a)(3)(iii) and does not mention or settle applicability to operations under Part 135.\",\"support_refs\":[\"statement\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[]},{\"question_id\":\"q4\",\"conclusion\":\"unknown\",\"answer\":\"The supplied material does not mention the phrase 'notwithstanding any other requirement' or address whether conditions of child-restraint permissions may be ignored.\",\"support_refs\":[\"statement\"],\"remaining_uncertainty\":[\"The phrase 'notwithstanding any other requirement' and its legal effect are absent from the provided text.\"]}]}",
